{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory was highly actionable and safely navigated the family through same-day high-risk obstetric review, levothyroxine bridging, thyroid testing, fetal monitoring, and final home safety-netting. However, RC4 was not fully met because the doctor never explained that NIPT is only a screening test and cannot replace prenatal diagnosis or exclude all genetic/structural problems, despite repeatedly addressing fetal brain ventricle/hydrocephalus uncertainty. Under the frozen rubric, that minor responsibility-chain omission caps the grade at 2 even though multiple high-order actions were otherwise completed.",
